 There are no signed builds yet: when they come, Windows SmartScreen and macOS Gatekeeper will warn before the first run.
 
+### Installing a release
+
+Builds are on the [Releases](https://github.com/tuliocll/lilac/releases) page.
+
+- **Windows:** unzip it anywhere and run **`lilac.exe`**. You'll see a second file, `launcher.exe`: that's normal.
+  `lilac.exe` is the app itself (backend, interface and icon all packed inside), and `launcher.exe` is the small helper
+  tinyjs uses to draw the window with WebView2. It doesn't do anything on its own, but `lilac.exe` needs it, so keep
+  both in the same folder. Shortcuts and pins should point at `lilac.exe` (pinning the open window works too).
+- **macOS:** open the `.dmg` and drag Lilac to Applications. Everything lives inside `Lilac.app`.
+- **Linux:** extract the `.tar.gz`; same idea as Windows — run `lilac` and keep `launcher` next to it.
+
 ## Why tinyjs?
 
 Picking [tinyjs](https://tinyjs.app) was **an experiment**: a ~6 MB desktop runtime with a JavaScript backend
